<!--
    UEFI protocol interfaces, service-table globals and the PEI and SMM phases
    (`option uefi on|off`).

    Stage P1 external-refinement. Four EDK2 modules:
    - uefi_diskio_x64.efi: DiskIoDxe (edk2-stable202505, OvmfX64 RELEASE_GCC5),
      a DXE driver that locates one protocol and installs three;
    - uefi_fv/StatusCodeHandlerPei.efi and uefi_fv/ReportStatusCodeRouterPei.efi
      (same build): two PEIMs, the first locating the PPI the second installs;
    - uefi_fv/TcgMorLockSmm.efi (edk2-stable202502, OvmfX64 with SMM, as
      shipped in Debian's ovmf 2025.02-8): an SMM driver.
    uefi_fv/kuna-uefi.index is what `kuna unpack` with its protocols flag writes
    for the three modules of that directory.

    Pass 1 (`uefi off`, the bug): a function other than the entry calls a boot
    service through an offset off an untyped global, and its parameters are
    untyped words.
    Pass 2 (default, the fix): the globals the entry stores the tables in are
    gST and gBS, a protocol lookup types its interface from the GUID, the
    installed instances and the functions they point at carry the interface's
    struct and member names, the PEIM is entered as a PEIM and its PPI lookup
    names the module that installs the PPI, and the SMM driver reaches its
    services through gSmst.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
